; Every *-msil triple selects the MSIL target, whatever its architecture
; (Design.md 3, decision D4), and the native CPU and feature strings that clang
; attaches for the native ABI are accepted silently (decision D7): no 'is not a
; recognized processor/feature' warning, and the output is the ILAsm module of
; ImplementationPlan.md 5.1 with no GNU assembler directive (recon
; asmprinter.md 12.2; '.data cil' is a legal ILAsm directive, so '.data' is
; only rejected on its own). The declarations below are not referenced, so the
; module is just the header.

